## Notes
- Screenshot is 1440x900 CSS pixels and shows the whole 50,000-rectangle document (world
  8000x4500, 16:9 like the canvas) with no letterbox; the mobile 390x844 layout has no
  horizontal overflow (documentElement.scrollWidth == innerWidth). The camera clamps at zoom
  0.1, so at 390 px the view crops the document; the caption names the document, not the
  drawn subset.
- The helper pauses the loop through window.__enginePlayground before capture, so the fps
  label in the PNG matches the value logged above (3 fps desktop, 12 fps mobile in this run).
- The headless browser renders WebGL with SwiftShader, so these fps values are a functional
  check only; performance numbers belong to P2-04 on the recorded hardware.
